Thought: Now that I have consolidated the data, I need to prepare it for ML training by creating a tabular dataset with advanced feature engineering, as specified in the input parameters.
Action: prepare_tabular_dataset
Action Input: {"polymorphs_json_path": "/Users/n0w0f/1_ml_claude_react/ml_nitrides_trial_9/consolidated_nitrides.json", "output_path": "ml_data", "target_property": "formation_energy_per_atom", "feature_engineering": "advanced", "test_split": 0.2, "normalize": true}

Thought: Now I'll train the XGBoost model using the prepared dataset with the specified hyperparameters (n_estimators=200, max_depth=8, learning_rate=0.1, subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_alpha=0.1, reg_lambda=0.1)
Action: train_xgboost_model
